  "question": {
    "text": "In van dar Wall equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi></math> is pressure, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is universal gas constant and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is temperature. The ratio of constants <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is dimensionally equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
